      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Response",
      "Anchor": "sample-response",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Step 1: Getting a Refresh Token",
        "Sample Response"
      ],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Sample Response",
      "Anchor": "sample-response",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Step 1: Getting a Refresh Token",
        "Sample Response"
      ],
      "Text": "Refresh tokens are approximately 500 characters long. We recommend that your application stack be made to handle tokens of at least 1000 characters to accommodate future expansion plans. This applies to access tokens as well as refresh tokens.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "Step 2: Exchanging a Refresh Token for a New Access Token",
      "Anchor": "step-2-exchanging-a-refresh-token-for-a-new-access-token",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Step 2: Exchanging a Refresh Token for a New Access Token"
      ],
      "Text": "You can exchange the refresh token for a new access token by making the following HTTP POST request with a Content-Type header of x-www-form-urlencoded and the following parameters in the request body:",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "code",
      "Section": "Step 2: Exchanging a Refresh Token for a New Access Token",
      "Anchor": "step-2-exchanging-a-refresh-token-for-a-new-access-token",
      "SectionPath": [
        "Introduction",
        "Step 2: Exchanging a Refresh Token for a New Access Token"
      ],
      "Text": "https://www.linkedin.com/oauth/v2/accessToken",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
